  "articleBody": "When you're diving into a kitchen refresh for a foreclosed property, it's easy to get excited about the cosmetic changes and overlook some crucial steps. One of the biggest mistakes we see is starting with those cosmetic upgrades – like painting cabinets or replacing countertops – before fixing any underlying issues. You absolutely need to address leaks, mold, or electrical problems first. Trust me, putting a fresh coat of paint over mold doesn't make it go away! Another common pitfall is underestimating hidden damage. What looks fine on the surface might have water damage or structural issues lurking behind cabinets or under sinks. It's smart to do some test demolition or thorough inspections to really see what you’re working with. And don't skip testing the systems! Make sure the plumbing, electrical, and appliances are all in good working order before you commit to a specific kitchen scope. Failing to do this upfront can lead to costly surprises and delays later on. Always choose a contractor who emphasizes a thorough inspection process and clearly explains what’s included and excluded in your project. HH Remodeling LLC always takes this careful approach to ensure a smooth renovation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
